      "provenance": {
        "notes": "CONFLICT on cats: the ASPCA lists the plant non-toxic to dogs, cats and horses; NC State flags it as a problem for cats (mild to moderate stomach upset), but ties the concern to the seeds, which houseplants never produce. Kept the higher grade for cats (1) per rule 5; to be decided by a reviewer. The dog entry rests on ASPCA alone. NC State also says the seeds are possibly toxic and carcinogenic for people, not graded. Watering: both pages say keep damp and well-drained, so keep_moist. Size is the RHS pot figure (up to 1.5 m, spread up to 0.5 m); NC State says 6 to 8 ft indoors. Humidity: thrives in humid air, no number."
      },
